{"archetypes":[{"name":"state-machine","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff changes /design review-loop continuation, caps, counters, and Gate C flow across scripts and docs.","prompt_body":"Investigate the Step 3 and Step 3.5 state-machine behavior across the changed /design scripts and skill prose. Focus on whether review-round-count persistence, cap handling, explicit approve stops, degraded-panel continuation, tally-error rollback, and per-round auto-apply semantics remain consistent across normal and failure paths. Check for mismatches between emitted env fields and the callers or harnesses that consume them. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"artifact-accounting","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff changes final-summary finding counts and introduces cumulative accepted-findings artifacts.","prompt_body":"Review the Plan review finding-count logic and related artifact lifecycle changes. Focus on whether FINDING_ and OOS_ block counting works with current artifact grammar, missing optional files, cumulative versus per-round files, duplicate headings across rounds, and empty/degraded outcomes. Also check that tests reflect realistic accepted-plan-findings artifacts rather than overfitting to narrow fixtures. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"workflow-contracts","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The implementation spans runtime scripts, skill instructions, approval-gate docs, and relevant-check routing.","prompt_body":"Examine whether the runtime behavior, operator-facing skill text, approval-gate reference docs, and relevant-check target routing describe and enforce the same workflow contract. Pay special attention to stale single-pass or per-tier cap language, missing harness routing for newly introduced scripts, and any contract drift between docs and executable behavior. Treat documentation changes as part of the shipped runtime surface where they guide agent control flow. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
